# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled test binaries — a STRUCTURAL rule, not a name list.
#
# Every runner in this repo compiles `<name>.zer` to an extension-less `<name>`
# beside it, so under a test tree "has no extension" IS the definition of a
# build artifact. Verified exhaustively before this rule replaced the hand-kept
# list it supersedes: all 565 such tracked files were ELF, with no exceptions.
#
# The old list was a deny-list of individual binary names, which is the shape
# this project keeps replacing with gates: it required an edit per new test and
# silently tracked ~560 binaries that nobody had gotten round to adding. A rule
# that holds by construction needs no maintenance and cannot drift.
#
# `!<dir>/*.*` keeps the sources; the trailing `!<dir>/*/` keeps subdirectories
# (rust_tests/qemu) from being swept up with them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/zer/*
!tests/zer/*.*
tests/zer_fail/*
!tests/zer_fail/*.*
tests/zer_trap/*
!tests/zer_trap/*.*
tests/zer_gaps/*
!tests/zer_gaps/*.*
tests/zer_proof/*
!tests/zer_proof/*.*
test_modules/*
!test_modules/*.*
rust_tests/*
!rust_tests/*.*
!rust_tests/*/
zig_tests/*
!zig_tests/*.*

